id: E14847-draft-2501_91199785
trigger_tool: unix-socket|conan|consumer-test
phase: testing|runtime
error_signature: "AF_UNIX pathname bind denied in writable HMDFS or cache directory|sockaddr_un.sun_path too long|daemon unavailable for client handshake"
severity: 2
category: af-unix|filesystem|consumer-test
match_keywords: AF_UNIX, sockaddr_un, sun_path, HMDFS, bind EPERM, native private temporary directory, mock daemon, bounded handshake
title: Verify AF_UNIX directory capability and use a bounded task-private native socket handshake
root_cause: >
  A client library may require a daemon socket while the real daemon is absent
  from the test host. An absolute Conan cache path may exceed sun_path, and a
  convenient /tmp pathname can be refused by the target security policy. A
  short relative pathname avoids length overflow but not filesystem/socket policy:
  a writable HMDFS build directory can still reject bind. The test needs a short
  unique directory on native application-private storage plus bounded peer waits.
affected_scope: AF_UNIX client libraries tested on sandboxed OHOS targets without their production daemon
verification_cmd: "create a unique native private directory; bind and listen; invoke the installed client API; verify request/response bytes, bounded peer waits and close semantics; remove only the owned socket and directory"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: native-private-socket-with-bounded-protocol-faithful-test-peer
rec_description: >
  On OHOS use a unique mkdtemp directory under application-private files storage,
  not the HMDFS build cwd or cache TMPDIR, and supply its short socket path through
  the library's documented override. Bound accept readiness and read/write waits;
  join the peer on every started-thread path and report the exact failing syscall.
  Verify the real protocol and remove only owned resources. A bind failure is FAIL,
  never a passed or skipped test.
rec_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: "replace the AF_UNIX client with a no-op mock or claim hardware device input works"
forbid_1_reason: a fake return value cannot prove the packaged client protocol or real device capability
similar_to: E024, E341-draft-BBEA
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E14847-draft-2501_91199785.md
